Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 11:37:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/38] fix(verimark): backfill description + username on
 enroll-time FpPrint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`delete_enrolled_fingers` in fprintd is called at the start of every
new enroll to clean stale device-side prints. It iterates the user's
cached FpPrints (deserialized from disk) and logs metadata via g_log
before calling our delete() vfunc. NULL description / username from a
previously-enrolled print crashes the logger (strlen on NULL).

The fprintd CLI only sets `finger` and `username` on the template it
hands to libfprint — never `description`. Backfill both fields (if
absent) at enroll-complete time so the serialized print on disk
always has them populated for future iterations.

Note: existing cached prints from BEFORE this fix still have NULL
description and will keep crashing fprintd until they are deleted
manually (`rm /var/lib/fprintd/<user>/Kensington_VeriMark_DT/*`).

Drafted with AI assistance.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index ac3cab20..4f286625 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -1244,6 +1244,16 @@ static void verimark_enroll(FpDevice *device)
         fpi_print_set_type(template, FPI_PRINT_RAW);
         fpi_print_set_device_stored(template, TRUE);
         g_object_set(template, "fpi-data", data, NULL);
+        /* fprintd serializes the FpPrint to disk and later iterates the
+         * cached prints during enroll cleanup (`delete_enrolled_fingers`),
+         * logging metadata via g_log. A NULL description or username
+         * crashes that logger (strlen on NULL). The CLI only sets
+         * finger + username, so we backfill description here ; defensive
+         * username default if the caller didn't set one. */
+        if (fp_print_get_description(template) == NULL)
+            fp_print_set_description(template, "Kensington VeriMark DT");
+        if (fp_print_get_username(template) == NULL)
+            fp_print_set_username(template, "verimark");
         fpi_device_enroll_complete(device, g_object_ref(template), NULL);
     } else {
         /* Defensive fallback : if libfprint didn't hand us a template
